  "title": "file: We know compression type at cf_open",
  "description": "Since we know the file type after wtap_open_offline is called, we\nmust also know the compression type. Otherwise the magic numbers\nor heuristics wouldn't work to identify the file type. (We don't\nuse the extension in either case.) We definitely don't know any\n*more* at the top of cf_read than we do in cf_open after calling\nwtap_open_offline. However, when reading files from a live capture,\nwe call cf_open but not cf_read.\n\nSo we can retrieve and set it in cf_open and rescan_file, not just\nin cf_read, which is necessary in order to record the compression\ntype of a file if we ever support dumpcap directly writing compressed\nfiles on the fly. (#9311)",
  "state": "merged",
